|passage=We have to wait until they're ready to receive us, and make sure we turn up at the '''appointed''' time.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250926183046/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/technology/11216699/Art-on-demand-makes-emperors-of-us-all.html|archivedate=26 September 2025}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[name]] (someone to a [[post]] or [[role]]).
#: {{syn|en|make|name|designate|nominate|institute}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Numbers|4|19|passage=''Aaron and his shall go in, and '''appoint''' them every one to his service.''}}
#* {{RQ:NYPost|date=November 3 2014|author=Fredric U. Dicker|title=[http://nypost.com/2014/11/03/author-of-democrats-threatening-letter-identified/ Cuomo appointed 'vote or else' strategist]
|passage=Neal Kwatra, '''appointed''' by Cuomo to be the state Democratic Party's chief campaign strategist, was identified by two key Democratic insiders[...]}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[furnish]] or [[equip]] (a place) completely; to [[provide]] with all the [[equipment]] or [[furnishings]] necessary; to [[fit out]].
#* {{RQ:Lawrence Lady Chatterley's Lover|X|151|passage=It was a handsome old stucco hall, very elegantly '''appointed''', for Winter was a bachelor and prided himself on his style; but the place was beset by collieries.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Donald Olson|title=Germany for Dummies
|passage=The hotel is beautifully designed and beautifully '''appointed''' in a classic, modern style that manages to be both serene and luxurious at the same time.}}
