# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To make a [[firm]] [[decision]] to do something. To become [[determined]] to reach a certain [[goal]] or take a certain [[action]].
#: {{ux|en|I '''resolve''' to finish this work before I go home.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Charles Johnstone|title=The Reverie; or, A Flight to the Paradise of Fools|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=1mAzAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA202|volume=2|location=Dublin|publisher={{...|Printed by}} Dillon Chamberlaine|year=1762|page=202|oclc=519072825|passage=At length, one night, when the company by ſome accident broke up much ſooner than ordinary, ſo that the candles were not half burnt out, ſhe was not able to reſiſt the temptation, but '''reſolved''' to have them ſome way or other. Accordingly, as ſoon as the hurry was over, and the ſervants, as ſhe thought, all gone to ſleep, ſhe ſtole out of her bed, and went down ſtairs, naked to her ſhift as ſhe was, with a deſign to ſteal them {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To determine or decide in purpose; to make ready in mind; to fix; to settle.
#: {{ux|en|He was '''resolved''' by an unexpected event.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|act=I|scene=i|lines=50–51|page=210|column=2|passage=Gentlemen, importune me no farther, / For hovv I firmly am '''reſolu'd''' you knovv: / That is, not to beſtovv my yongeſt daughter, / Before I haue a husband for the elder: {{...}}}}
# To come to an [[agree]]ment or make [[peace]]; patch up relationship, settle differences, bury the hatchet.
#: {{ux|en|After two weeks of [[bicker]]ing, they finally '''resolved''' their differences.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive|reflexive}} To break down into [[constituent]] parts; to [[decompose]]; to [[disintegrate]]; to return to a simpler [[constitution]] or a [[primeval]] state.
#: {{ux|en|The House immediately '''resolved''' itself into a Committee on the Bill.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet|act=I|scene=ii|passage=O, that this too too solid flesh would melt, / Thaw, and '''resolve''' itself into a dew!}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Indian Emperour|page=15|passage=And ye Immortal Souls, that once vvere Men, / And novv '''reſolv’d''' to Elements agen.}}
# To cause to perceive or understand; to acquaint; to inform; to convince; to assure; to make certain.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1596|author=w:Walter Raleigh|title={{w|The Discovery of Guiana|The discovery of the large, rich, and beautiful Empire of Guiana, with a relation of the great and golden city of Manoa}}
|passage=In health, good air, pleasure, riches, I am '''resolved''' it cannot be equalled by any region.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Divorce|book=9|passage=We must be '''resolved''' how the law can be pure and perspicuous, and yet throw a polluted skirt over these Eleusinian mysteries.}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Riches|page=16|passage='''Reſolve''' me Reaſon, vvhich of theſe is vvorſe, / VVant vvith a full, or vvith an empty purſe: {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Fielding Tom Jones|passage=She was proceeding in this manner when the surgeon entered the room. The lieutenant immediately asked how his patient did. But he '''resolved''' him only by saying, "Better, I believe, than he would have been by this time, if I had not been called; and even as it is, perhaps it would have been lucky if I could have been called sooner."}}
# {{lb|en|music}} To cause a [[chord]] to go from [[dissonance]] to [[consonance]].
# {{lb|en|optics}} To render visible or distinguishable the parts of something.
# {{lb|en|computing}} To find the [[IP address]] of a [[hostname]], or the entity referred to by a [[symbol]] in [[source code]]; to [[look up]].
# {{lb|en|rare|transitive}} To [[melt]]; to [[dissolve]]; to [[liquefy]] or [[soften]] (a [[solid]]).
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|passage=With milke-white Hartes vpon an Iuorie ſled, / Thou ſhalt be drawen amidſt the froſen Pooles, / And ſcale the yſie mountaines lofty tops: / Which with thy beautie will be soone '''reſolu’d'''.}}
# {{lb|en|rare|intransitive|reflexive}} To [[melt]]; to [[dissolve]]; to become liquid.
#* {{RQ:Arbuthnot Aliments
|passage=When the blood stagnates in any part, it first coagulates, then '''resolves''', and turns alkaline.}}
